    {
      "id": 90,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "START HERE: corrected motion control",
      "pos": [
        0,
        -500
      ],
      "size": [
        810,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 7,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "b1a247c9cf9dbfda4b2c0a0c1d50950667eeaa0c"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Load two photos of the SAME replacement character and the source MP4. Set source start/window, then run. Source aspect is automatic. This graph uses native Fun ControlNet Union 2.0 with per-frame SDPose body/hands, not just a video reference.\n\nNo Ollama or Reference Pack. No Turbo. Existing full BF16 H3 weights. First run the separate PREVIEW graph, or switch node 11 to Preview motion only. All large H3 loaders depend on that gate. Inspect Source_vs_Pose: broken skeletons or the wrong performer cannot be repaired by a stronger prompt.\n\nSource/ref/control/output all share one exact 24-fps frame count. Default 5.25-second window produces 124 frames when available (5.167 seconds); a 15-second source yields 345 frames (14.375 seconds). A source/window of at least 15.084 seconds can supply 362 frames (15.083 seconds). No missing tail is invented."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Load two photos of the SAME replacement character and the source MP4. Set source start/window, then run. Source aspect is automatic. This graph uses native Fun ControlNet Union 2.0 with per-frame SDPose body/hands, not just a video reference.\n\nNo Ollama or Reference Pack. No Turbo. Existing full BF16 H3 weights. First run the separate PREVIEW graph, or switch node 11 to Preview motion only. All large H3 loaders depend on that gate. Inspect Source_vs_Pose: broken skeletons or the wrong performer cannot be repaired by a stronger prompt.\n\nSource/ref/control/output all share one exact 24-fps frame count. Default 5.25-second window produces 124 frames when available (5.167 seconds); a 15-second source yields 345 frames (14.375 seconds). A source/window of at least 15.084 seconds can supply 362 frames (15.083 seconds). No missing tail is invented."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 91,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "QUALITY / LIMITS",
      "pos": [
        900,
        -500
      ],
      "size": [
        810,
        390
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "b1a247c9cf9dbfda4b2c0a0c1d50950667eeaa0c"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Default control strength 1.0 for all denoising steps, 40-step res_multistep/beta, guidance 1 via BasicGuider. If the pose preview is correct but output still drifts, compare the SAME seed at strength 1.15, then 1.3. Higher strength is not automatically better and can distort identity.\n\nHands and body are controlled; dense face landmarks are OFF to reduce source-face transfer. The original video remains a scene/camera/clothing reference. This is NOT a pixel-locked background replacement or exact optical-flow retiming. Source identity, occlusions, fast cuts and invisible limbs can still cause errors.\n\nFull BF16 plus ControlNet on an A100 80 GB needs offloading and remains unbenchmarked. Preprocessing models are unloaded before H3. Keep the 1 MP native canvas and short default clip first. Check generated face AND motion. Rebuild the H3 image and prepare HMOTION models before loading this JSON."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "Default control strength 1.0 for all denoising steps, 40-step res_multistep/beta, guidance 1 via BasicGuider. If the pose preview is correct but output still drifts, compare the SAME seed at strength 1.15, then 1.3. Higher strength is not automatically better and can distort identity.\n\nHands and body are controlled; dense face landmarks are OFF to reduce source-face transfer. The original video remains a scene/camera/clothing reference. This is NOT a pixel-locked background replacement or exact optical-flow retiming. Source identity, occlusions, fast cuts and invisible limbs can still cause errors.\n\nFull BF16 plus ControlNet on an A100 80 GB needs offloading and remains unbenchmarked. Preprocessing models are unloaded before H3. Keep the 1 MP native canvas and short default clip first. Check generated face AND motion. Rebuild the H3 image and prepare HMOTION models before loading this JSON."
      }
    }
